From: Mateus Lima Alves <mateuslima.ti@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: add the RTL8367RB

The RTL8367RB (chip number 0x6000, version 0x1000) belongs to an older
family than the chips this driver supports, but the registers it uses
are the same, the indirect PHY access for registers 0-31 reaches the
same address and it speaks the same CPU tag protocol. Add it with its
two RGMII external interfaces and the init jam of the vendor rtl8367b
driver, which also patches the PHYs.

Unlike the newer chips, it reads its reset register as 0 while it
resets and ignores writes until it is done, so polling that register
ends at once and the whole setup is lost: every PHY then reads 0.
Wait the full second that the Realtek documentation gives for the
reset on this chip.

Signed-off-by: Mateus Lima Alves <mateuslima.ti@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
@@ -633,6 +633,63 @@ static const struct rtl8365mb_jam_tbl_entry rtl8365mb_init_jam_8365mb_vc[] = {
 	{ 0x13F0, 0x0000 },
 };
 
